.TH VIMTUTOR 1 2026-10-31 "w64devkit" "w64devkit Manual"
.SH NAME
vimtutor \- start the Vim tutor on a scratch copy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vimtutor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vimtutor
starts
.BR vim (1)
on a new copy of the Vim tutor, a lesson file to read and edit, so the
original is never changed.
The copy is a file in the directory named by
.BR TMP ,
named
.B tutor
followed by a random number, and it is not deleted afterwards.
.PP
Vim runs with
.BR "\-N \-u NONE" ,
so it is not Vi compatible and reads no initialization files.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.B vimtutor
is a batch file that ignores its arguments.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMP
The directory for the copy.
.TP
.B PATH
Where
.B cmd.exe
finds
.BR vim .
.SH NOTES
Only the English tutor is installed, and there is no
.B \-g
option to use gvim.
This page replaces the upstream
.B vimtutor
page, which describes the Unix shell script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vim (1)
